    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72844.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "Well, there will be a number of amendments to try to shift some of the funding. From my perspective, we have already cut 23 billion, which we needed to do given our debt situation. But 16 billion or about two thirds of the cuts are from the farm programs. And in fact, the farm programs are only 14% of the bill. And I think people don't always know that. And one of the reasons we were able to get such a strong vote is that we're able to keep the support of conservation groups. 640 conservation groups are supporting this bill, as well as the nutrition groups with the school lunch program and other things. But I think people need to remember us. They will clearly put an amendment to shift things and to get rid of parts of the bill. They have to remember that the bulk of the cuts nearly two-thirds of them came on the farm end to the 14 percent of the bill that the farm program.",
