  {
    "episode_id": 72844,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72844.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Again, I want to look at each amendment and there's still people who are working on amendments and other things. I like our farm bill as it is. In the past I have been an advocate for reforms. I was someone that put forward a reform idea last time to direct payments. And I think it got a majority of the senators but didn't beat the filibuster. But now we've gotten rid of direct payments. And so those direct payment reforms are no longer relevant. I'm sure there'll be attempts on crop insurance. I just want to make sure that whatever changes if any are made, that it keeps the bill strong enough that we have broad support in the farm state so we can move this forward and move it forward in the house.",
