  {
    "episode_id": 72844,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72844.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "You know, I don't think there's anything much to do with an election cycle as much as it has to do with the cycle of the farm bill. That farm bill has to be reauthorized because if we don't have a new farm bill, we literally are going to go into next year. No one knows what will happen. because of the fact that we always have a farm bill in place. One of the best things about the economy in a very challenging time has been rural America. When you look at Minnesota, we're down to 5.6% unemployment. A lot of that has to do with our ag economy and how that feeds into companies like General Mills and Land of Lakes and Hormol and others. We are well aware of the fact that's important for our economy, for the rural areas, and that's what brings us to this timing, not the election cycle. The only way the election cycle plays in as far as I'm concerned is that it gets harder and harder to do stuff as it gets closer to the election, so it would be much better to get this done this summer and get the Senate bill done in the next week or two and then move it right over to the House so that they can get something done and then we could get a conference committee done before August.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The farm bill needs to be reauthorized.",
        "confidence": 0.97
      },
      {
        "text": "Without a new farm bill, uncertainty exists about future policy and operations.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "Rural America has played a strong role in economic stability during challenging times.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Minnesota’s current unemployment rate is 5.6%.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "The agricultural economy contributes significantly to major companies like General Mills, Land of Lakes, and Hormel.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "The importance of the farm bill is tied to its impact on rural economies and national industry.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The timing of farm bill action is driven by economic necessity rather than the election cycle.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "Legislative progress becomes more difficult as elections approach.",
        "confidence": 0.87
